# https://github.com/browserslist/browserslist#readme
#
# CAUTION — queries are combined with OR: version lines ADD browsers, they
# never cap anything. The `not` lines below are what actually enforce the
# floor; without them, `>= 0.5%` and `last 2 major versions` pull Chrome 109,
# Safari 15.6, Firefox 121 and Samsung 23 back in.
#
# Floor required by the CSS we actually ship — the PostCSS pipeline only runs
# autoprefixer + postcss-custom-media, so nothing is transpiled:
#   CSS Nesting                → Safari 16.5+ / Chrome 112+ / Firefox 117+
#   Relative color oklch(from) → Safari 16.4+ / Chrome 119+ / Firefox 128+ / Samsung 25+
#   Media range (width >= )    → Safari 16.4+
#
# Coverage: 90.04%

>= 0.5%
last 2 major versions
not dead

Chrome >= 120
Firefox >= 128
iOS >= 16.5
Safari >= 16.5
Samsung >= 25

# Effective floor — counters the OR semantics of the queries above
not chrome <= 119
not safari <= 16.4
not ios_saf <= 16.4
not firefox <= 127
not samsung <= 24

# Legacy / proxy browsers: no CSS variables, no clamp(), no @layer
not Explorer <= 11
not op_mini all
not and_uc <= 15.5
not and_qq <= 14.9
not kaios <= 3.1 # fix floating label issues in Firefox (see https://github.com/postcss/autoprefixer/issues/1533)
